/**
 * Role-based access control: the single source of truth.
 *
 * - Permissions are granular strings; roles are bundles of permissions.
 * - Firebase custom claims carry only `role` (claims are capped at 1000 bytes),
 *   and every enforcement point derives permissions from this file:
 *   proxy (route access), Server Actions (`requirePermission`) and Firestore
 *   rules (generated by `npm run rules:generate`).
 *
 * Keep this module free of runtime imports so scripts can load it directly.
 */

